 1
Write a PL/SQL program that prompts for EMPNO, ENAME and SAL.
If EMPNO does not exist in EMP table then INSERT the record.
Otherwise UPDATE ENAME and SAL for that EMPNO.
(Control Structures)
====================================================================

SQL Command:
------------

sql> ACCEPT P_EMPNO PROMPT 'Enter Employee Number : '
sql> ACCEPT P_ENAME PROMPT 'Enter Employee Name   : '
sql> ACCEPT P_SAL   PROMPT 'Enter Salary          : '

sql> DECLARE
       V_COUNT NUMBER;
     BEGIN
       SELECT COUNT(*)
       INTO V_COUNT
       FROM EMP
       WHERE EMPNO=&P_EMPNO;

       IF V_COUNT=0 THEN
          INSERT INTO EMP(EMPNO,ENAME,SAL)
          VALUES(&P_EMPNO,'&P_ENAME',&P_SAL);

          DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Employee Inserted.');

       ELSE

          UPDATE EMP
          SET ENAME='&P_ENAME',
              SAL=&P_SAL
          WHERE EMPNO=&P_EMPNO;

          DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Employee Updated.');

       END IF;

       COMMIT;
     END;
     /

Output (Case-1):
----------------

Enter Employee Number : 8001
Enter Employee Name   : JACK
Enter Salary          : 6500

Employee Inserted.

PL/SQL procedure successfully completed.


Output (Case-2):
----------------

Enter Employee Number : 7369
Enter Employee Name   : SMITH
Enter Salary          : 5000

Employee Updated.

PL/SQL procedure successfully completed.


