 3
Write a PL/SQL program that prompts for EMPNO and updates
salary based on the following conditions:

DEPTNO=10  -> Salary +10%
DEPTNO=20  -> Salary +15%
Other Dept -> Salary = Salary + COMM
(Control Structures)
====================================================================

SQL Command:
------------

sql> ACCEPT P_EMPNO PROMPT 'Enter Employee Number : '

sql> DECLARE

       V_DEPTNO EMP.DEPTNO%TYPE;

     BEGIN

       SELECT DEPTNO
       INTO V_DEPTNO
       FROM EMP
       WHERE EMPNO=&P_EMPNO;

       IF V_DEPTNO=10 THEN

          UPDATE EMP
          SET SAL=SAL*1.10
          WHERE EMPNO=&P_EMPNO;

       ELSIF V_DEPTNO=20 THEN

          UPDATE EMP
          SET SAL=SAL*1.15
          WHERE EMPNO=&P_EMPNO;

       ELSE

          UPDATE EMP
          SET SAL=SAL+NVL(COMM,0)
          WHERE EMPNO=&P_EMPNO;

       END IF;

       COMMIT;

       DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Salary Updated.');

     END;
     /

Output:
-------

Enter Employee Number : 7782

Salary Updated.

PL/SQL procedure successfully completed.


