 4
Create MYTABLE1 with RESULT column and write a PL/SQL program
to insert values from 1 to 10 except 6 and 8.
(Control Structures)
====================================================================

Create Table:
-------------

sql> CREATE TABLE MYTABLE1
     (
         RESULT NUMBER
     );

Output:
-------

Table created.


PL/SQL Program:
---------------

sql> BEGIN

       FOR I IN 1..10 LOOP

          IF I=6 OR I=8 THEN
             CONTINUE;
          END IF;

          INSERT INTO MYTABLE1
          VALUES(I);

       END LOOP;

       COMMIT;

     END;
     /

Output:
-------

PL/SQL procedure successfully completed.


Verify:
-------

sql> SELECT * FROM MYTABLE1;

Output:
-------

RESULT
------
1
2
3
4
5
7
9
10

8 rows selected.

